-- `@lang` declares the language a module is written in — the language an
-- untagged `@nlg` in it carries. It means exactly what tagging every herald
-- would mean, which is the point: one declaration instead of one tag per
-- rule.
--
-- A herald that names its own language still wins for that language, so a
-- Hebrew module can carry English renderings without declaring anything else.
@lang he

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is large` @nlg %amount% עולה על הסף
                  @nlg:en the claim of %amount% exceeds the threshold
  IF amount GREATER THAN 100

-- No English rendering here: asking for English falls back to this one, so a
-- partly translated module still produces a whole document.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is small` @nlg %amount% קטן מן הסף
  IF amount LESS THAN 10

#EVAL `is large` 150
#EVAL `is small` 5
